  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: Which of the given reagents is used to prevent the hydrolysis of
    Al3+ ions?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: Dilute sulphuric acid is an acid that is added to the reaction
    mixture to prevent the hydrolysis of aluminium ions.Distilled water can not be
    used as it will support hydrolysis The 1:1 water + alcohol mixture is used to
    wash the crystals, and can not be used to prevent the hydrolysis of aluminum
    ions.
  options:
  - Distilled water
  - Dilute sulphuric acid
  - 1:1 water + alcohol mixture
  - None of these
  correctOptionIndex: 1
